cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this release, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Rigorous Certification and Spectral Analysis of 1,000,000 Riemann Zeta Zeros"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-18"
type: dataset

authors:
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Rashad"

abstract: >
  This release presents a reproducible computational certification and numerical
  analysis of the first 1,000,000 nontrivial Riemann zeta zero entries. The package
  includes FLINT/Arb ball-arithmetic certification, Hilbert-space spectral modeling,
  GUE spacing and CDF comparisons, Montgomery/GUE pair-correlation analysis,
  spectral staircase analysis, prime-error reconstruction, zero-count sensitivity
  ladders, figures, checksums, and a final report. This is not a proof of the
  Riemann Hypothesis.

keywords:
  - Riemann Hypothesis
  - Riemann zeta function
  - zeta zeros
  - computational number theory
  - FLINT
  - Arb
  - ball arithmetic
  - GUE
  - random matrix theory
  - pair correlation
  - spectral staircase
  - prime counting
  - explicit formula
  - Hilbert-Polya

license: "CC-BY-4.0"
